<title>FRANCE: LVMH will not drop DFS deal - source.</title>
<headline>LVMH will not drop DFS deal - source.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>French leisure group LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton said it had no intention of backing out of a $2.47 billion deal to buy a 58.75 percent stake in San Francisco-based duty free retailer DFS Group Ltd.</p>
<p>A source close to the French company said that Kohlberg Kravis Roberts &amp; Co had written to DFS's four controling shareholders saying it was willing to bid, provided LVMH withdrew from its deal.</p>
<p>The source said she had seen a copy of the letter sent to the DFS controling shareholders.</p>
</text>
